22. SINGLE AGENT VS RCR
============================================================

RCR = Research → Critique → Refine


Single Agent:

Advantages:
- Faster
- Cheaper
- Simple

Best For:
- Simple tasks
- Quick responses
- Low-latency applications


RCR Pattern:

Advantages:
- Better quality control
- Better completeness
- Structured improvement
- Clear separation of responsibilities

Best For:
- Research
- Analysis
- Important reports
- High-quality outputs


Main Trade-Off:

Single Agent
    ↓
Faster + Cheaper
    ↓
Potentially Lower Quality


RCR Pattern
    ↓
Better Quality Control
    ↓
More Processing + Higher Cost


============================================================
23. WHEN TO USE RCR
============================================================

USE WHEN:

- Quality is critical
- Accuracy is important
- Completeness matters
- Research is complex
- Output will be published or shared
- Iterative improvement is useful


DON'T USE WHEN:

- Task is simple
- Instant response is required
- Latency must be very low
- Cost is highly constrained
- Additional refinement provides little value


